  "instruction": "The image has no internet. A local wheelhouse is at `/home/user/Desktop/wheels`; it contains `scikit-fem` 12.0.2 and its `scipy` 1.13.1 dependency.\n\n1. Install scikit-fem from the wheelhouse into your Python environment, for example with `python3 -m pip install --user --no-index --find-links wheels scikit-fem==12.0.2`.\n2. Solve the Poisson problem on the unit square [0,1] x [0,1]: `-Delta u = 2*pi^2*sin(pi*x)*sin(pi*y)`, with u = 0 on all edges. The exact solution is u = sin(pi*x)*sin(pi*y); its maximum is 1.\n3. Deliver in /home/user/Desktop:\n   - `solve.py` - the script that computes the solution with scikit-fem and writes the summary; it must import `skfem`.\n   - `summary.txt` - one number: `max_u`, the maximum nodal value of the computed solution.\n\nThe evaluator checks that solve.py uses scikit-fem and that max_u is within 2% of 1. Do not hard-code the answer.",
